    "narrative": "The core of the LawDog lineup today rests on the favorable matchup against Javier, providing the primary catalyst for our offensive output. **Bryce Harper** (75.63) stands as the undeniable pillar of the lineup, benefiting from a soft xERA of 4.49 and a strong 3-hole placement that maximizes his RBI and run-scoring potential. **Luis Arraez** (67.29) and **Justin Crawford** (63.31) also see significant value spikes against the same starter. **Justin Crawford** remains critical to our strategy; despite hitting 8th, his elite speed profile provides the necessary legs to chase stolen bases, which remain our scarcest category. Meanwhile, **Daulton Varsho** (48.64) and **Cal Raleigh** (42.78) face stiffer competition against Wheeler and deGrom, respectively, dragging their efficiency scores toward the marginal threshold despite their positional utility.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Braden Montgomery**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 39.36. While he holds intriguing upside, the combination of a tough matchup against Jones and his current projected output fell just below our strict 40.0 floor for active starts. We are opting to keep him on the bench to preserve our limited game caps rather than force an inferior statistical profile. Elsewhere, the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Lawrence Butler** due to scheduled off-days forces us to rely on the depth of the remaining roster. We remain wary of **Cal Raleigh**\u2019s outlook; his base projection is solid, but the negative impact of facing deGrom\u2014combined with a park penalty\u2014suggests his production will likely be suppressed today. Keep a close eye on the late-breaking weather reports, as the elite nature of the opposing arms, particularly deGrom and Wheeler, creates a high-variance environment that could render even our top-tier plays difficult to project.",
